# LeakSanitizer suppressions for third-party runtime libraries.
# Keep dsd-neo-owned leaks unsuppressed.
#
# Matched by module, so only allocations whose stack passes through the named
# library are dropped: a leak in project code that merely reaches one of these
# is still reported.

# fontconfig caches its pattern and charset objects for process lifetime and
# frees none of them. Anything that renders text pulls this in - here it is the
# Qt Quick tests, via Qt's font database - and it is reached before main(), so
# no project code owns the allocation or could release it.
leak:libfontconfig
